 `run_native_smoke.py` is now an executable native entry. Its CLI requires `--asset`, `--admission` (the exact native actuation result), `--standing-source`, `--standing-one`, `--standing32`, `--bindings`, and fresh `--output`; actual runtime additionally requires `--device cuda:0 --headless`. `--preflight-only` validates all source/admission bytes using standard-library code and cannot start Isaac. `canonical_direct_ppo.native_contract.verify_inputs(args)` and `validate_result(directory, identity)` are the host composition APIs. A host should import this unique package with the preparation directory on its path, not load a relative-import module under an unrelated bare name. No host or guard is added here.
 
-The versioned entry adapter currently targets frozen standing source `f81f61d257cb92b65ad80f3b7d27c45497e66254092e244a32da02555b11e2a4`. It compiles the complete verified module and replaces exactly its post1000-control reporting tail. All native scene/import/reset/servo/400Hz loop and original exception/finally statements remain byte identical. Exact helper paths stay active through lazy imports and foreign cached modules are rejected. This is explicitly an adapted entry, not a claim that the old standing entry itself ran PPO. A changed standing runtime requires a reviewed successor binding before dispatch.
